id: pm-review-closeout-verification
title: Verify closeout evidence and detect gamed gates
description: "Independently evaluate acceptance criteria against fresh linked tests, linked artifacts, comments and change baselines. Emit compact verdicts without closing items."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T15:11:44.530Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T08:57:51.419Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T08:57:51.403Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T11:05:18.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Closeout reports each criterion with concrete evidence and fails closed on gaps; detects weakened gates and skipped focused deleted or ineffective tests; supports plain trackers and optional isolated behavioral revert checks; demonstrates three merged fleet items and a seeded gamed change; unchanged npm and Bun release gates pass
resolution: "Delivered by https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/25 (merge 260d41c13b4e, head a405f62ac6a5)"
expected_result: Closeout reports each criterion with concrete evidence and fails closed on gaps; detects weakened gates and skipped focused deleted or ineffective tests; supports plain trackers and optional isolated behavioral revert checks; demonstrates three merged fleet items and a seeded gamed change; unchanged npm and Bun release gates pass
actual_result: "Merged at 2026-10-22T11:05:18Z; no readable required checks, so every completed head check run had to succeed, be neutral or be skipped; successful checks: CodeQL, CodeRabbit, codeql, cubic · AI code reviewer, test (22), test (26)"
comments[32]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T15:11:53.850Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked: pm help exposes linked-test execution but no independent criterion verification; pm-ops verify-release executes package gates and assurance measures thresholds; pm-lint validates context quality and explicitly does not certify evidence; pm-context assembles handoff evidence. pm-review owns the independent closeout verdict. Design: conservative criterion binding to fresh named test results, typed gate findings, git baseline or recorded linked-file state, isolated optional source revert. No automatic closure."
  "2026-10-21T15:21:21.114Z",codex-agent,"Initial behavioral acceptance now passes: a plain tracker proves a named criterion from a fresh run and becomes sensitive after source-only restore; a vacuous passing test is flagged source_unexecuted and revert_survived. Source item bytes remain unchanged. The pinned host rejects universal read-output controls on test mutations; the runner omits those controls. Full release coverage and three merged-item demonstrations are next."
  "2026-10-21T15:35:03.650Z",codex-agent,"Three exact-merge read-only demonstrations complete: PR 16 round-exit-contract: 2 unproven (120-second test budget exceeded); PR 15 f82w: 2 unproven (no linked tests); PR 12 respond: 16 unproven (combined original linked commands exceeded 120 seconds). All refuse closeout, preserve original criteria and leave tracked source state unchanged. Seeded vacuous test returns source_unexecuted and revert_survived; legitimate no-git evidence proves its criterion. Details: docs/closeout-dogfood.md. Continuing unchanged-threshold release gates."
  "2026-10-21T15:38:39.402Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral proofs passed in disposable source copies: disabling only detectGaming caused its regression to fail (exit 1, assertion failure); disabling only checkInvocation caused the real-tracker vacuous-test regression to fail (exit 1, missing source_unexecuted). Original source untouched. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance passed 1/1, including closeout JSON/TOON success and unproven exit 1. Added detached-descendant timeout regression and recognition for Node spec/Bun stderr assertions. Release checks remain pending."
  "2026-10-21T15:42:00.712Z",codex-agent,"Fresh linked pm test execution passes 2/2 commands after clearing the inherited PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT in the disposable child host. The nested host previously selected the outer workspace instead of the copy. The regression injects a wrong outer workspace and also removes git from PATH. The tracker has test-result-tracking disabled, so the PM run returns tracking_disabled rather than persisting a test_runs row; this comment records the observed result without changing project policy."
  "2026-10-21T15:49:25.557Z",codex-agent,"First full npm release check measured every authored source at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines and zero duplication, but failed the pre-existing classifier wall-clock assertion: 63.60046 ms versus the unchanged 50 ms limit. The isolated single-test rerun passed 1/1. This is not a passing release gate. Bun and isolated-HOME runs on code commit 92f1c29 are pending; a complete npm rerun will retain the same thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T15:53:53.457Z",codex-agent,"Bun source coverage passed 150/150 with 100 percent in all four dimensions; later release stages are still running. The isolated-HOME source suite passed 149/150 and exposed an immediate-process-state race in the new SIGKILL regression. The test now observes bounded eventual termination (at most two seconds), without changing runtime code, the cleanup deadline, classifier limit or coverage floors. It still fails if the detached descendant remains live. Targeted cleanup regression passes."
  "2026-10-21T15:55:48.994Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding note: the first targeted cleanup invocation failed because a broad import replacement also modified generated fixture strings, and the shell continued into the note and commit. That failed invocation is not passing evidence. Fixture strings are now corrected; build:test and the targeted detached-descendant cleanup regression both pass. Future evidence-recording command sequences fail immediately on a failed check. Original append-only history is retained."
  "2026-10-21T16:03:26.016Z",codex-agent,"Added and passed two real-tracker copy regressions: canonicalize a symlink workspace root before preparing the disposable copy, and refuse external artifact symlinks in source/tracker snapshots. Disabling only the new artifact-link guard in a separate source copy makes the refusal regression fail with an assertion error (exit 1). TypeScript test build, lint and zero-duplication checks pass. Final gates are restarted for this runtime change; previous candidate gates are not approval for this head."
  "2026-10-21T16:14:07.091Z",codex-agent,"CI reproduced a real installed-consumer gap: PM-managed extensions contain a node_modules SDK peer symlink, and the artifact-link guard incorrectly refused that declared dependency. A real-tracker dependency-link regression failed before the fix (exit 1, assertion error) and now passes, together with workspace-alias and external-artifact refusal regressions (3/3). The tracker snapshot preserves links only within managed extension node_modules; artifact links remain refused. Build:test, lint and zero duplication pass. Final packed acceptance and all release gates are being rerun; prior and canceled checks are not approval."
  "2026-10-21T16:36:46.332Z",codex-agent,"Revised focused suite passes 24/24 with zero skipped tests. Positive fixtures now use the production-default 60-second execution budget: full-source concurrent runs exceeded their artificial 20-second fixture budget. Dedicated deadline/output-limit regressions, the existing 50 ms classifier limit, and all coverage/lint thresholds are unchanged. Latest standalone packed npm/native-Bun acceptance passes 1/1 on local Bun 1.3.5; CI uses Bun 1.4.3 and still refuses preparation in its native-Bun consumer. An isolated matching Bun runtime is being used for diagnosis; no host runtime was replaced. Failed and incomplete release runs remain non-approval."
  "2026-10-21T16:39:12.296Z",codex-agent,"The matching Bun 1.4.3 runtime and fresh installed consumers pass locally, including a Node 26 linked command, while CI still reports a preparation refusal. Added bounded preparation phase/error categories to identify the failing stage without exposing paths or raw output. Pure diagnostic regressions and TypeScript test build pass. Positive fixture budgets remain bounded at the existing production default; classifier and coverage thresholds are unchanged. No failed CI result is treated as approval."
  "2026-10-21T16:44:25.445Z",codex-agent,"CI phase diagnostics identify the remaining refusal as workspace-copy/Error, while matching local Bun consumers still pass. Artifact policy refusals now carry a stable category and workspace-relative artifact identity so CI can identify the rejected link without exposing absolute paths. The external-artifact refusal regression, test compilation and lint pass. The gate remains blocked pending that concrete result."
  "2026-10-21T16:49:09.472Z",codex-agent,"CI identified the refused artifact as a Bun package download-cache symlink under .bun/install/cache. Added an exact-layout real-tracker regression: it fails before the fix (exit 1, assertion error) and now passes. Source snapshots exclude .bun, .npm and .cache alongside existing dependency/build caches; installed dependency bindings stay available, while external artifact links remain refused. Cache/dependency/artifact regressions pass 3/3; build:test, lint and zero duplication pass at unchanged thresholds. Final complete gates are restarting for this concrete fix."
  "2026-10-21T17:07:34.428Z",codex-agent,"Correction: the earlier statement that the PM-linked run passed 2/2 was based on the selected-command count, not its exit status. The saved progress log actually reports command 1 failed and command 2 passed. The latest PM-linked run likewise fails command 1, despite standalone and CI passes. Those PM-linked runs are not passing evidence. Investigating inherited source-context restrictions in nested execution, then rerunning and checking both process exit status and every command status. Original append-only receipts are retained."
  "2026-10-21T17:16:24.795Z",codex-agent,"The nested-run failure is confirmed trust_refusal: fixture command intake inherited the parent repository source root, so its metadata recorded the parent branch although its own tracker has no git. A regression forcing parent intake context failed before the fixture fix and now passes. Fixtures bind intake to their real workspace; production trust checks are unchanged and no untrusted-command override is used. The detached-child test also gives startup five seconds before triggering its cleanup deadline, while still requiring bounded termination; a loaded host previously killed the launcher before its pid file existed. Dedicated short-budget assertions and all coverage/classifier thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T17:33:19.826Z",codex-agent,"Verified final PM-linked run: process exit 0; both progress receipts explicitly report end status=passed and exit_code=0. Main integration command completed in 552937 ms; evidence-boundary command completed in 4757 ms. The verification script also asserted exactly two passed command receipts and no failed receipt. No timeout failures occurred. Durable run recording remains disabled by project policy, so this comment preserves the observed result. CI on ca837cc is green for Node 22/26 and full native Bun release gates; isolated-HOME npm gate is still running."
  "2026-10-21T17:38:24.988Z",codex-agent,"The final isolated-HOME npm run on ca837cc exited 1: 154/155 source tests passed, zero skipped, all 26 authored sources still measured 100 percent in all four dimensions. The existing severity-parsing adversarial-input test hit its unchanged 5000 ms child-startup deadline (ETIMEDOUT). CI Node 22/26 passes the identical test. This failed local gate is not approval. Retrying with an installed Node 26 runtime matching the CI major, with identical source and thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T18:03:13.086Z",codex-agent,"Final complete isolated-HOME npm release:check on ca837cc with Node 26 exited 0. Outer source suite: 155 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; all 26 authored sources met unchanged 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines; duplication 0 percent; production audit 0 vulnerabilities. All later stages passed, including changelog and attestation checks and packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1. CI Node 22/26 and full Bun 1.4.3 release:check are also green at this code/test head. Final PM-linked run independently passed both commands with verified exit 0. Three original merged-item copies remain unproven 2/2/16; the gamed seed is blocked. Known boundaries and failed-run corrections remain in linked docs and append-only history. Handing off for independent orchestrator review; item stays in progress and will not be closed."
  "2026-10-21T19:15:07.534Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 25: all three unresolved threads verified valid (PRRT_kwDOVGABD86u6Tae, PRRT_kwDOVGABD86u6Tau, PRRT_kwDOVGABD86u6Ta1). Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Branch contains main and matches remote. Fix direct-root clone detection, disable rename collapsing, retain opaque repository entries with skip receipts. Self-review also guards opaque tests, invocation and revert baselines. Only targeted regressions, typecheck and lint run locally on the loaded host; full unchanged npm and Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-21T19:18:12.642Z",codex-agent,"Targeted regression suite passes 4/4 (0 failed, 0 skipped). npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass. npm ci completed with 0 vulnerabilities. The first typecheck attempt ran before dependency installation completed and could not find tsc; retry after installation passed. Initial nested fixture inherited parent-branch provenance and was refused by the unchanged pinned host trust checks; the regression now models pre-existing branch-independent plain-tracker evidence placed beneath a repository. Such evidence executes and proves its criterion after the root-only clone fix. Branch-bound provenance remains governed by host trust policy. No dist files are tracked. Whole PR reviewed for clone/discovery, rename and opaque-evidence handling; same-class opaque test/invocation/revert paths are covered. Function-only behavioral revert checks are next."
  "2026-10-21T19:21:22.052Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof complete: six separate function-only reversions, retaining the regression tests, each exited 1 with AssertionError. executeCloseout reversion (required hasGit import restored) breaks nested plain-tracker execution at workspace-root; closeoutChanges reversion loses renamed test/source paths; a separate closeoutChanges reversion throws on opaque binary entries; detectGaming reversion fails opaque-test blocking; checkInvocation reversion falsely accepts opaque native invocation; reviewCloseout reversion attempts the opaque source baseline and fails the inconclusive-verdict assertion. All functions restored immediately after their individual proof. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern \"a plain tracker\" test/closeout-review.test.ts; same command with patterns \"staged and committed\", \"opaque repository entries\" (state and detector proofs separately), \"opaque source\" (invocation and revert proofs separately). No build/import failures count as proof. The original opaque-state proof also reproduced the domain binary exception; assert.doesNotThrow now makes that contract explicit. Fixed-source PM-linked targeted run and existing no-git/Git copy smoke regressions are running."
  "2026-10-21T19:22:40.332Z",codex-agent,"Fixed-source verification after all six revert proofs: PM-linked targeted run ./node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-review-closeout-verification --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 exited 0; selected command end status=passed and exit_code=0, all four review regressions pass, 0 failed/0 skipped and all failure categories 0. Existing smoke command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"plain tracker fresh evidence|no-git tracker works|git-backed execution\" test/closeout.test.ts passes 3/3, 0 failed/0 skipped. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass after sharing the existing intake-context helper. PM durable run recording remains disabled by project policy; observed command receipt is recorded here. No local full release gates were run in this round. All thresholds and dependency pins remain unchanged; pushing code plus append-only tracker evidence for CI npm/Node 22, npm/Node 26 and Bun release validation."
  "2026-10-21T19:33:09.842Z",codex-agent,"CI passed on code head 184455141ea236c3101a19704fc2a2bf3cca0551: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/39661345623 . Node 22 npm gates and Node 26 npm gates each pass 159/159 source tests, 0 failed, 0 skipped, all 26 authored sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines. Full bun run release:check also passes 159/159 with the same unchanged thresholds. Packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx consumer acceptance passes 1/1 in each Node job and 1/1 in the Bun release gate. PM health, identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, duplication (zero clones), docstrings, audit, package, changelog and publish-attestation checks are green. The latest review refresh still has only the original three threads and no newer review body. No local timeout occurred in this round; the pre-install tsc absence passed after installation. Releasing the claim while leaving the item in_progress. This receipt-only handoff commit will receive its own CI run before final reporting."
  "2026-10-21T19:38:30.610Z",codex-agent,"Final self-review found an additional same-class edge case: opaque baseline bytes can equal the placeholder string, so generic before===after shortcuts could skip changed tests/source or exclude them from revert analysis. Reclaimed the item to make opaque status authoritative before equality checks and extend the existing regressions with a placeholder collision plus a separately comparable source change. Previous green gates remain valid only for the prior code head; new source will receive targeted proofs and fresh CI. No thread interaction or lifecycle closure."
  "2026-10-21T19:40:26.557Z",codex-agent,"The opaque-placeholder collision is fixed in detectGaming, checkInvocation and the source-restore selection. The strengthened fixture uses baseline bytes equal to the marker and a second comparable source change whose assertion would fail on restore, so ignoring the opaque source cannot accidentally yield a sensitive verdict. PM-linked targeted run passes 4/4, 0 failed/skipped, selected command status passed and exit 0; all failure categories 0. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass. Repeating the original six function-only revert proofs against the strengthened tests and adding three collision-specific function reversions against f8305d3. Existing Git/no-git smoke results remain applicable; source preparation and fixture helper behavior are unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T19:42:24.564Z",codex-agent,"Final strengthened revert proofs pass 9/9: original six function-only reversions against df7164a each exit 1 with AssertionError, plus detectGaming, checkInvocation and reviewCloseout reversions against f8305d3 each exit 1 with AssertionError on placeholder collisions. The collision reviewCloseout proof fails because an incorrectly ignored opaque source lets the separately comparable source produce a false sensitive verdict. Exact additional commands: node --test --test-name-pattern \"opaque repository entries\" test/closeout-review.test.ts (detectGaming); node --test --test-name-pattern \"opaque source\" test/closeout-review.test.ts (checkInvocation and reviewCloseout independently). All source functions restored in finally blocks. Strengthened fixed-source PM-linked run already passed all 4 tests, all failure categories 0; typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. Publishing code/tests/docs and append-only PM evidence for fresh full CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T19:53:30.248Z",codex-agent,"Strengthened code head 4a157d02d43a7d4c8c9186483f66c50eef64eec7 passes full CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/39664090295 . Node 22 npm gates, Node 26 npm gates and full bun run release:check each pass 159/159 source tests, 0 failures/skips, with all 26 authored sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance passes 1/1 in each gate. All PM health, identity/privacy, lint, typecheck, zero-duplication, 82-declaration docstring, audit, package, changelog and attestation checks pass at unchanged thresholds and pins. The nine behavior-only revert proofs and fixed-source 4/4 PM-linked regressions are recorded above; the earlier 3/3 Git/no-git smoke results remain applicable. No local timeout occurred in this round. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress. The receipt-only handoff commit will receive fresh CI before final reporting; no source changes remain."
  "2026-10-21T21:15:19.467Z",codex-agent,"PR 25 review round: inspected all six unresolved threads with complete comment pagination and the latest CodeRabbit body (no outside-diff or nitpick additions). All six findings are valid. Fix policy-name false positives, UTF-8 stream decoding, canonical sandbox paths, root-only cache exclusions and missing runner receipts; relabel historical dogfood validation. Self-review the full diff, add targeted regression and behavioral revert evidence, and use CI for unchanged full npm/Bun release gates due to host load. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-21T21:21:20.418Z",codex-agent,"All six review findings fixed. Self-review additionally anchored package.json as a complete basename and corrected native coverage containment for workspace names beginning with two dots. Six new regressions pass through the pinned PM runner (6/6, zero failures/skips; tracking_disabled policy unchanged). The initial broader targeted run passed 35/36 and exposed an interaction between root-only cache exclusions and managed tracker dependency links in the first workspace copy; a shared copy-policy helper now preserves the existing managed-link exception in both copies while refusing other artifact symlinks. Rerunning the affected dependency/cache/artifact smoke tests and final revert proofs. The first nested-dependency fixture used unsupported TypeScript inside node_modules; corrected to JavaScript. The final fixture asserts file presence before loading it, so a reverted snapshot filter yields a named assertion failure rather than a module-load error. No timeout failure so far. No thresholds or dependency pins changed; no dist files are tracked."
  "2026-10-21T21:22:45.146Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification: pinned PM command npx --no-install pm test pm-review-closeout-verification --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 exits 0; node --test test/closeout-round.test.ts passes 6/6, zero failures/skips. Existing affected smoke command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"PM-managed extension dependency links|linked external artifact|package-manager and tooling caches\" test/closeout.test.ts passes 3/3. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run build pass. Eight final isolated revert proofs retain the tests and each exit 1 with ERR_ASSERTION: policy, UTF-8, sandbox path, cache scope, runner receipt, native path containment, historical document labeling and managed tracker links. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern \"policy names\" test/closeout-round.test.ts; same file with patterns \"split UTF-8\", \"symlinked temp\", \"nested cache names\" (cache and containment independently), \"forged named output\", \"historical validation\"; node --test --test-name-pattern \"PM-managed extension dependency links\" test/closeout.test.ts. Each mutation restores only its affected behavior in detectGaming, boundedHost, executeCloseout or recordExecution (or the historical document), in disposable source copies. The refined cache proof produces a failed named file-presence assertion, not an import/build error. All originals are untouched. Earlier 35/36 broad targeted result and fixture correction remain non-passing historical evidence. No load timeout occurred in this round. Full release gates are delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T21:28:13.124Z",codex-agent,"CI green on source head 5981758306308ec7ab49094dc106e66d980d9a15: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/39678352298 . npm release-gate steps on Node 22 and Node 26 each pass 165/165 outer source tests, zero failures/skips, all 26 authored sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines. Full bun run release:check also passes 165/165 at the unchanged thresholds. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance passes 1/1 in each gate. Duplication is zero (0/6086 lines, 40 sources, zero clone pairs); all 82 declarations across 26 authored files are documented. PM health/history, identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, audit, package, changelog and attestation steps pass in both fresh CI clones. Optional local pm health reported ambient pm-github host skew (pinned host 2026.10.18 versus installed extension host 2026.10.21) plus an existing stale-item advisory; no pins, telemetry, histories or extension configuration were changed to hide it. Final review refresh has the same six original unresolved threads with complete comments and no newer CodeRabbit review body; no outside-diff or nitpick additions. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Releasing the claim while leaving the item in_progress for orchestrator verification; the receipt-only final commit will receive its own full CI run."
